comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T00:20:00.805Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status PM search for audited extension settings mutation found related closed workspace-audit and SDK audits but no current owner of this missing host-bound contract. GitHub #1345 cites pm-presets pm-1vx6 in that package's tracker; that is a separate consumer defect."
  "2026-09-29T04:56:31.683Z","harness:codex","Test-audit contract: a copied extension with no locally resolvable pm SDK can atomically mutate governed settings through its injected host SDK while retaining strict workspace history. Existing direct SDK singleton tests do not prove extension portability or failure compensation. Primary proof will use a disposable packed consumer."
  "2026-09-29T06:50:38.926Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: extension command SDK now exposes mutateWorkspaceSettings with a fixed host tracker path, lock-scoped read/validate/write, workspace history, author attribution, dry-run, and replay-safe operation IDs. Copied extension integration runs without a local SDK and passes strict health/history verification. Source-level tests cover preview, replay, no-op, invalid current/result, drift, and history failure compensation. Linked tests passed; full suite 9414 passed; exact V8 coverage 100/100/100/100; pnpm quality:static passed. Public SDK surface snapshot acknowledges the added host capability and optional controls."
  "2026-09-29T07:17:18.090Z","harness:codex","PR #1348 review follow-up: the host SDK now keys settings retries by registered command and operation ID; completed retries do not re-run extension code. Settings mutations use the standard serializer and emit onWrite after changed writes. Focused unit and installed-extension integration tests exercise cross-command IDs, legacy format and collection normalization, and hook behavior. pm-test-audit: each case checks externally observable state or history and would fail against the reviewed implementation; no implementation-only assertions or duplicated happy-path coverage."
  "2026-09-29T07:30:33.241Z","harness:codex","SDK surface review: the replay receipt now exposes an explicit replay variant with no callback-derived result, and createExtensionCommandSdk accepts optional command context. sdk/public-surface.json records both signatures with a breaking-change acknowledgement because the snapshot classifier treats signature changes conservatively; existing three-argument callers remain executable."
  "2026-09-29T08:09:24.196Z","harness:codex","Final PR #1348 review verification: all 9414 tests passed, exact V8 coverage is 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts, pnpm quality:static passed including exported docstrings and 97.88% mutation score, pnpm security:scan passed, and both linked test commands passed in schema-sandboxed pm test. A fresh npm-packed archive installed in /tmp/pm-1348-packed-aE4P4Y, where npx and bunx reported 2026.9.29 and strict health returned zero findings. Installed-extension acceptance verifies independent same-ID commands, inert replay, serializer normalization, and changed-write hook delivery."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T06:50:39.821Z","harness:codex",Copied extensions must receive governed workspace mutations through host-injected SDK services; resolving local SDK packages or writing settings.json directly breaks portability and audit attribution.
